---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy"
  updated="18 October 2026"
  summary="What Resurface stores about you, why, and who else can see it."
>
  <div class="legal-callout">
    <p>
      <strong>In short.</strong> Resurface stores your account, your study
      progress and the questions you make, plus a few records needed to run the
      service. There are no analytics or advertising trackers, and nothing is
      sold. Material you upload is sent to Google&rsquo;s AI to write your
      questions, so do not upload anything confidential. You can delete your
      account, and everything in it, from Profile at any time.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Resurface is a revision platform for UK medical students, run by a small
    independent team. For anything in this policy, including requests to see or
    delete your data, email{" "}
    <a href="mailto:hello@tryresurface.com">hello@tryresurface.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we store</h2>
  <p>Only what the app needs in order to work. Everything below is tied to your account.</p>

  <div class="legal-table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>What</th><th>Why</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Email address</td>
          <td>To sign you in, confirm your account and reset your password.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Display name and profile photo</td>
          <td>To show who you are on the leaderboard and on decks you share. The photo is optional and only ever one you upload yourself.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Your answers, and whether you got them right</td>
          <td>To schedule your reviews and show your progress.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Review schedule, streak, daily goal, saved questions and settings</td>
          <td>To decide what to show you next and keep the app as you set it.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Your decks and the questions you generate, write or edit</td>
          <td>So they are there whenever you sign in.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Questions you report, and anything you write with the report</td>
          <td>So we can fix the question.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Reminder settings, if you turn reminders on</td>
          <td>The time you chose, your time zone and your browser&rsquo;s push address, so we can send one reminder a day.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    We do not store your password. Sign-in is handled by Supabase, which keeps
    only a cryptographic hash of it. If you sign in with Google, we receive your
    email address and name, never your Google password, and Resurface has no
    access to your Gmail, Drive, contacts or calendar.
  </p>

  <h3>Records we keep to run the service</h3>
  <p>These never include the content of your questions or answers.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>AI usage:</strong> each time Resurface asks the AI to generate
      questions or explain one, we record that it happened, for which account,
      and how much of the AI it used. This is how we stay within our limits.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Deck sharing:</strong> when you open someone&rsquo;s share link,
      add their deck, or get new questions from it, we record who shared it, who
      received it, which deck, and when.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Loading times:</strong> how long the app took to load for you, and
      whether you were on a phone or computer, so we can find what makes it slow.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What we do not collect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>No analytics or advertising trackers, on the website or in the app.</li>
    <li>No location, contacts or device fingerprinting.</li>
    <li>
      No health information about you. Resurface contains medical study
      material; it never asks for anything about your own health.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who can see what</h2>
  <p>
    Your answers, scores, schedule and decks can be read only by your own
    account. This is enforced by the database itself, not just by the app.
    The exceptions are things you choose to share:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The leaderboard.</strong> Other signed-in users see your display
      name, your photo if you have one, how many questions you answered this week
      and your streak. Never your scores or which questions you got wrong. You can
      leave the leaderboard at any time in Profile.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your profile photo.</strong> It is stored so that it can be shown
      on the leaderboard, which means anyone with its direct link could view it.
      You can remove it in Profile.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Decks you share.</strong> Anyone with the link sees the deck, its
      questions and your display name, and can add a copy to their account.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Decks Resurface features.</strong> If we feature a deck you made
      for everyone to use, with your agreement, all users see it with your name
      on it.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Resurface&rsquo;s administrators can see account details (names, email
    addresses, when people joined and how much they use the app) to run the
    service, deal with reports and remove anything inappropriate. We do not look
    at individual answers.
  </p>

  <h2>The AI, and what you should not upload</h2>
  <p>
    When you use Generate, the material you upload or paste (Anki decks, slides,
    PDFs, notes or images) is sent to Google&rsquo;s Gemini AI so it can write
    questions from it. When you use Resurface AI, the question, its options, the
    answer you picked and the messages you type are sent. Your name, email
    address and study history are never sent.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Resurface currently uses Google&rsquo;s free tier, and you should
    know what that means:</strong> Google may use what is sent through it to
    improve its products, and people at Google may review it. So do not upload or
    type anything confidential, and never anything that could identify a real
    patient. Lecture slides and your own notes are fine.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Resurface keeps one thing in your browser that works like a cookie: a sign-in
    token, so you do not have to log in on every visit. It also remembers small
    preferences on your device, such as night mode. None of this is used to track
    you, there are no third-party cookies, and that is why there is no cookie
    banner.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else processes your data</h2>
  <p>
    We use a small number of providers to run Resurface. They act on our
    instructions and may not use your data for their own purposes, except Google
    as described above.
  </p>
  <div class="legal-table">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Provider</th><th>What they handle</th><th>Where</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Supabase</td><td>Accounts, sign-in, the database, and profile photos</td><td>Ireland (EU)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Vercel</td><td>Hosting the website, the app and its server</td><td>EU and US</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Google</td><td>Writing questions and explanations from what you send (Gemini), and Google sign-in if you use it</td><td>US</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Resend</td><td>Sending sign-in codes, confirmation emails and, if you opt in, news and study emails</td><td>EU and US</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Your browser&rsquo;s push service</td><td>Delivering reminders, if you turn them on (Google, Apple or Mozilla, depending on your browser)</td><td>Varies</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Emails</h2>
  <p>
    We send account emails, such as sign-in codes and confirmations, because the
    service needs them. News, tips and study emails are sent only if you opted in,
    and you can opt out in Profile or from any of those emails.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    For as long as you have an account. You can delete your account yourself in
    Profile, which removes your profile, photo, decks, questions and study data
    straight away. Backups are overwritten on a rolling basis and are fully
    cleared within 90 days. The operational records above may be kept after that,
    but with nothing left that links them to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under UK data protection law you can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to
    correct or delete it, or object to how we use it. Email{" "}
    <a href="mailto:hello@tryresurface.com">hello@tryresurface.com</a> and we will
    reply within 30 days, free of charge. If you are unhappy with how we have
    handled your data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner&rsquo;s
    Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>, though we
    would rather you told us first so we can put it right.
  </p>

  <h2>Legal basis</h2>
  <p>
    We use your account, progress and decks because that is needed to provide the
    service you signed up for. We keep the operational records because we have a
    legitimate interest in running the service reliably and within its limits. The
    leaderboard, reminders and marketing emails rely on your choice to use them,
    which you can change at any time in Profile.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Resurface is for university students and is not meant for anyone under 16. If
    you think a child has made an account, tell us and we will remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes in a way that affects you, we will tell you in the app,
    not just update the date at the top of this page.
  </p>
</Legal>
